---
import { LINKS } from '../consts';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const roles = [
	{ title: 'Principal Product Engineer', org: 'Cogent Labs, Tokyo', dates: 'May 2026 – present' },
	{ title: 'Senior Software Engineer', org: 'Cogent Labs, Tokyo', dates: 'May 2024 – May 2026' },
	{ title: 'Backend Engineer', org: 'Cogent Labs, Tokyo', dates: 'Sep 2022 – May 2024' },
	{ title: 'Technical Project Manager, Backend Engineer', org: 'Desquared, Athens', dates: '2020 – 2022' },
];
---

<Base
	title="Work"
	description="Selected work by Thanos Theodosiou: product engineering on an AI document-processing platform at Cogent Labs in Tokyo."
>
	<h1>Work</h1>
	<p class="lede">
		Since 2022 I've worked at <a href="https://www.cogent.co.jp/">Cogent Labs</a> on SmartRead, an AI document-processing
		(OCR) platform used by 40+ enterprise organizations in Japan, first as a backend engineer, then as tech lead, now as
		Principal Product Engineer. A few stories from that time. The full history is in my <a href={LINKS.cv}>CV</a>.
	</p>

	<article class="story">
		<h2>Replacing the ML orchestration layer with zero downtime</h2>
		<p>
			<strong>Why it mattered.</strong> Model serving ran on a set of legacy "coordinator" services that were hard to
			change and expensive to operate, and every new model made it worse.
		</p>
		<p>
			<strong>What changed.</strong> I led the migration to a new model-serving orchestration architecture while
			customers kept processing documents. We cut over without downtime and removed more than ten services.
		</p>
	</article>

	<article class="story">
		<h2>From hackathon prototype to shipped product</h2>
		<p>
			<strong>Why it mattered.</strong> Customers had large archives of documents they had already OCR'd with us, but
			no good way to ask questions of them.
		</p>
		<p>
			<strong>What changed.</strong> A hackathon RAG prototype over OCR'd documents became Cabinet. I incubated it from
			the prototype into a shipped product.
		</p>
	</article>

	<article class="story">
		<h2>A feature that unlocked a ¥150M deal</h2>
		<p>
			<strong>Why it mattered.</strong> A large enterprise deal depended on a capability the platform didn't have yet.
		</p>
		<p>
			<strong>What changed.</strong> I shipped it, and the deal closed. Around the same time I built SmartRead+ and cut
			the first load of the verification screen, where operators spend most of their day, by up to 70%.
		</p>
	</article>

	<article class="story">
		<h2>Changing the foundations while shipping</h2>
		<p>
			<strong>Why it mattered.</strong> The platform needed to move from Datastore to Postgres and from GCP to AWS, and
			some customers run it on-prem in air-gapped environments, without the roadmap stopping.
		</p>
		<p>
			<strong>What changed.</strong> Both migrations landed alongside feature work. I also maintained the on-prem Go
			deployment on k3s and containerd, and made its images 60% smaller.
		</p>
	</article>

	<h2>Roles</h2>
	<ul class="roles">
		{
			roles.map((r) => (
				<li>
					<span>
						<strong>{r.title}</strong>, {r.org}
					</span>
					<span class="muted">{r.dates}</span>
				</li>
			))
		}
	</ul>
	<p class="muted small">
		B.Sc. Computer Science, University of Piraeus. Greek (native), English (full professional), Japanese (JLPT N3).
	</p>
</Base>
